 ## Background
-StereoGaussians was introduced in 2026 by authors associated with the "StereoGaussians: Feed-Forward 3D Gaussian Splatting from Stereo Images" paper [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Feed-forward Generalizable Reconstruction](23168-feed-forward-generalizable-reconstruction.md) and addresses the need for nearby-view extrapolation in stereo-camera applications [S1, unofficial]. It is trained on the SceneSplat-Stereo dataset, which pairs stereo inputs with nearby target views from 803 static scenes [S1, unofficial].
+StereoGaussians was introduced in 2026 by authors associated with the paper "StereoGaussians: Feed-Forward 3D Gaussian Splatting from Stereo Images" [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the principles of feed-forward 3DGS and leverages pretrained stereo networks (FoundationStereo) to predict Gaussian attributes. The method was trained on the SceneSplat-Stereo dataset, which pairs stereo inputs with nearby target views from 803 training scenes [S1, unofficial]. It is used on StereoNVS and ReplicaGS datasets [S1, unofficial].
 
